WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:25.029
INTRO:
Being a politician is extremely difficult.

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:29.710
Regardless of how fair, transparent, honest,
and well-spoken you are, roughly half the

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.560
population will always despise you simply
because both of you have fundamentally different

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.600
beliefs.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.660
Considering this, if you’re a politician,
you wanna make sure that you don’t wanna

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.960
piss off the side that supports you because
then you’re really screwed.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.530
As you can see from the clip though, that’s
exactly what UK’s prime minister Boris Johnson

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.789
has done.

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:54.339
Over the past couple of months, Johnson has
been flamed by basically everyone in parliament

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:57.370
including most of the members in his own party.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.780
In fact, 27 out of the 31 Scottish Conservative
MSPs, or basically representatives, have publicly

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.390
voiced their disapproval of Johnson.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:11.060
Likewise, Johnson’s public approval ratings
have never been more atrocious.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:17.290
At the peak of his unpopularity, 73% of adults
felt that Johnson was performing poorly.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.440
Considering this overwhelming negative feedback,
many members of Johnson’s inner circle have

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.740
already resigned like Allegra Stratton.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.390
Johnson, however, has bit his tongue and tried
his best to at least finish out his term.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:33.210
So, here’s what happened to Boris Johnson
and why the UK is demanding that he resign

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.960
as prime minister.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:41.490
1ST LOCKDOWN:
Taking a look back, the root of Johnson’s

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.390
unpopularity can be traced back to March 23,
2020.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:49.840
On this fateful day, the UK government issued
a strict stay-at-home lockdown across the

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:50.840
country.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.440
Restaurants, pubs, and non-essential retailers
were all told to close, and citizens were

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.909
restricted to traveling only to and from essential
work.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:03.540
But despite these strict orders for citizens
and businesses, it seems like Johnson and

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.030
his staffers felt that these rules did not
apply to them.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.009
In fact, many pictures and videos that would
eventually be leaked suggest that his inner

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:13.810
circle had little regard for these restrictions.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:18.130
The first example of this was a get-together
that took place on May 15, 2020.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:22.560
At the time, the official restrictions stated
that people had to maintain 2 meters worth

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.130
of social distancing and only a maximum of
2 people from different households were allowed

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.840
to meet in a public place.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.810
Judging from the picture though, about a dozen
people were meeting in the garden, no one

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.370
was wearing masks, and social distancing is
basically nonexistent.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.990
Johnson has insisted that this was simply
a business meeting, but the inclusion of his

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:44.090
wife in the meeting suggests otherwise.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:49.670
Moving forward 5 days, on May 20, 2020, Johnson’s
senior aide Martin Reynold’s invited roughly

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.069
30-40 staff members to a garden picnic.

00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:57.330
Two of these invitees were of course Johnson
and his wife Carrie who both attended.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.240
Reports suggest many of Johnson’s staff
members even advised him that this get-together

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.530
was in violation of lockdown restrictions.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:08.780
Yet, Johnson attended anyway and he has denied
receiving warnings about the party’s violations.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.890
Moving forward another month, we have Johnson’s
56th birthday which took palace on June 19,

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:14.890
2020.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.520
By this point, covid restrictions had been
lightened up a decent amount, and gatherings

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.330
up to 6 people were allowed outdoors.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.909
But for Johnson’s birthday, not only did
30 people gather which is 5 times the permitted

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:28.190
amount, but they would gather indoors.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:33.330
Fortunately, UK’s covid restrictions would
lighten up even more starting on July 17,

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.439
2020, so it seemed like these parties were
something that Johnson could leave behind

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:38.769
in the rearview mirror.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:42.810
In reality, though, the pandemic had just
begun.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.799
2ND LOCKDOWN:
As you guys now know, Covid cases would pick

00:03:47.799 --> 00:03:51.910
up once again in late 2020 as the world faced
a second wave.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:57.390
As a result, on October 31, 2020, Johnson
would announce a second round of strict lockdowns.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:02.159
Just like the first round, restaurants, pubs,
gyms, and nonessential retailers all had to

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:04.360
shut down for at least 4 weeks.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:09.019
Johnson went on to apologize that Christmas
may be very different that year and that he

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:13.519
hopes that taking early action can prevent
even more action from being required.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:18.510
Despite this somber speech, just 2 weeks later
on November 13, 2020, staff members would

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:22.990
reportedly attend a gathering with Carrie
Johnson at the prime minister’s residence.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:28.450
Similarly, just two weeks after this on November
27, 2020, a party would be thrown for Johnson’s

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.630
senior aide Cleo Watson, and Johnson would
even give a speech at this event.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:38.350
A few weeks later on December 14, 2020, Johnson’s
Conservative party would host a full-on party

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.720
at their HQ in Westminster.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.940
I think you get the gist of what’s going
on.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.980
While the nation was under strict lockdown,
Johnson and colleagues basically just continued

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.750
on with daily life.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.480
On December 17, 2020, a leaving party was
thrown at the Cabinet office.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.850
Similarly January 14, 2021, another gathering
was hosted to celebrate the departure of two

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:00.850
private secretaries.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:06.660
By this point, it was clear that Johnson didn’t
accidentally make a violation here or there.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:11.330
His colleagues and he were consistently violating
Covid restrictions week after week, but the

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.150
nail in the coffin didn’t come till April
16, 2021.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:19.530
This time, the Downing Street staff hosted
not one but two parties.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.740
Fortunately, Johnson did not attend either
of these and Covid restrictions were much

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.250
looser by this point and vaccines were pretty
readily available.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.810
But what made these parties fateful was their
ill timing.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.650
You see, just one week before these parties,
Queen Elizabeth II’s husband Prince Philip,

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.950
Duke of Edinburgh passed away on April 9,
2021.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:42.950
The funeral was planned for April 17, 2020,
which meant that the Downing street parties

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.320
took place the night before the funeral.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:50.240
For obvious reasons, much of the UK felt that
these parties were extremely distasteful and

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.540
disrespectful.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:55.180
This led to the press looking into the prime
minister’s history with parties, and their

00:05:55.180 --> 00:06:00.250
findings would annihilate Johnson’s reputation.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.180
EXPOSED:
Over the next several months, the media along

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:08.770
with investigators would uncover more and
more of the parties and gatherings we just

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.100
discussed, and the public would grow more
and more irritated with each discovery.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:18.250
But, the piece of evidence that sent the public
over the edge was a leaked video of Johnson’s

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:22.830
press secretary, Allegra Stratton, and a bunch
of her colleagues joking about a Christmas

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:47.690
business meeting and not following social
distancing.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:52.620
Shortly after this video was leaked, Allegra
would announce her resignation in tears.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.400
Many people in the comments have gone on to
claim that the tears are fake and that this

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.940
is terrible acting.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.810
But personally, I think the tears are in fact
genuine.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:06.000
However, like other comments have pointed
out, the tears are likely not because she’s

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.870
sorry for her mistake, but because she got
caught and is about to lose her job.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:14.770
After this video was leaked, Johnson had no
choice but to conduct an official investigation

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.020
into the matter.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.070
Johnson would task Cabinet Secretary Simon
Case with conducting the investigation, but

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:25.020
he would soon be replaced by civil servant
Sue Gray as it was uncovered that one of the

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.730
parties took place at Simon’s own office.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:31.190
Over the next month and a half, Sue would
conduct her investigation which uncovered

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:34.010
loads of quote “extremely damning” evidence.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:38.330
Sue apparently found dozens of photos showing
Johnson attending events with extremely loose

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.320
or no covid restrictions.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:44.490
But unfortunately, much of this evidence has
yet to be released, and it’s unclear if

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.650
it’ll ever be released.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:50.850
You see, Sue was supposed to publish her full
25-page report on the last week of January.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:56.210
But, on January 28, it was revealed that Sue’s
report would only be 11 pages long and that

00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:00.500
key details would be left out in order to
quote on quote avoid any prejudice to their

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.500
investigation.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.401
On top of this, Johnson got to review the
contents of the report for 3 days before it

00:08:05.401 --> 00:08:08.500
was finally published on January 31, 2022.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.761
Unfortunately for Johnson, some of the worst
public and political backlash we’ve seen

00:08:12.761 --> 00:08:16.730
in modern history would follow soon after.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:21.390
BACKLASH:
On the surface, it seems like people are pissed

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:25.530
that Johnson didn’t take Covid that seriously
when it comes to his personal actions.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:29.940
But, I think people’s distaste for Johnson
is much more deeprooted them him simply not

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.500
taking Covid seriously.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:36.090
A bunch of world leaders didn’t take the
pandemic that seriously, but they’re not

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:40.710
receiving the same backlash that Johnson is,
and I think the key reason for this is that

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.210
they were consistent, unlike Johnson.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.210
Take Trump for example.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.950
He didn’t take the pandemic too seriously
either.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:51.310
He often held massive gatherings at the White
House and he even held a rally with thousands

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:53.620
of people in June of 2020.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:58.490
While Trump did receive a lot of from the
media and democrats, republicans didn’t

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.460
exactly turn on him because he was consistent
with his messaging.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:05.780
Trump’s entire premise was that the illness
was here to stay and that everyone should

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:09.090
return to normal life including returning
to work and school.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:12.760
Whether you agree with this perspective or
not is besides the point.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.780
The point is that Trump practiced what he
preached.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.610
Johnson, however, did not.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:22.430
To please the media and a part of the public,
Johnson implemented severe covid restrictions,

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:25.320
but in his personal life, he didn’t follow
any of these.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:28.930
This left quite a sour taste in many British
people’s mouths as it felt like Johnson

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.810
and his colleagues thought that they were
above the law.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:35.600
While everyday citizens were limited from
going to work, attending school, and opening

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.150
up their local businesses, Johnson was behaving
like nothing was happening.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:43.250
What’s even more surprising though than
the public being upset is that politicians

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.770
are also upset.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.490
All the comments on the initial video I showed
you guys are gushing over how crazy it is

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.410
to finally see a politician being held accountable.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:55.600
And while I agree that it’s nice that Johnson’s
peers are calling him out on his actions,

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.990
I also think that many of them likely have
ulterior motives.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:03.280
Here’s the thing, prime ministers aren’t
directly voted for in the UK.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:07.130
Rather, British citizens vote for members
of parliament, and the leader of the majority

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.260
party becomes the prime minister.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:13.250
As a result, it’s the local elections that
determine the national leader.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:18.040
This might be a bit confusing because it’s
basically the opposite in the US.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.820
Americans mainly just vote for a president
and all of their local election choices are

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.070
just the candidates from the same party.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:28.360
As a result, it’s in American politicians’
best interest to align with the winning candidate.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:33.050
In the UK though, given that citizens don’t
vote for the prime minister directly, local

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:36.240
candidates don’t really care about aligning
with the prime minister.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:40.480
In fact, it would probably be beneficial for
them if Boris Johnson is ousted because it

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.570
gives them a chance to move up.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:46.730
With that being said, Johnson’s colleagues
turning on him may have more to do with politics

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.440
than serving justice.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.320
But hey, at least he’s being held accountable.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:57.030
END OF POLITICAL CAREER?:
At the end of the day, Johnson’s seemingly

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:00.920
elitist view along with his colleagues’
lack of dependence on him have really torn

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.660
apart Johnson’s reputation.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:07.480
But, Johnson has had one saving grace which
is Russia’s invasion of Ukraine.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:12.300
Russia’s invasion has turned international
attention away from Johnson and onto Putin,

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:16.540
Zelenskyy, Russia, Ukraine, NATO, and so on
and so forth.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:20.380
In other words, the severity of Putin’s
actions has made most people forget about

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.650
Johnson’s actions.

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:25.850
Aside from diverting attention, Russia’s
invasion has given Johnson the perfect opportunity

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:30.610
to redeem himself by supporting Ukraine, letting
in refugees, and acting as a western hero

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:38.350
in the war.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.610
All of his efforts seem to paying off as the
distaste for Johnson has noticeably declined

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:46.420
over the past 2 months from 73% down to 63%.

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:51.230
Johnson still has a lot of work to do to win
back support from his colleagues and the public.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.360
But given that UK’s next general election
is taking place till May 2, 2024, Johnson

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.470
has plenty of time to do damage control.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:03.120
Also, in terms of resignation, given that
Johnson hasn’t already resigned, it’s

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.040
extremely unlikely that Johnson will resign
due to PartyGate, and Johnson will likely

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.730
just finish out his term.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.110
But that’s just what I think.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:12.680
Do you guys think Johnson should be fired?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.880
Comment that down below.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:18.260
Also, drop a like if you think all politicians
need to be held more accountable.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:22.510
And of course, consider checking out our international
channels to watch our videos in other languages

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:28.820
and consider subscribing to see more questions
logically answered.

